A json run stopped by timeout now prints its result envelope instead of exiting with an empty stdout. It's committed as Part of #1221. Stream-json still has the same problem and stays open on #1221.

The bug: timeout 60 yoyo --output-format json -p … died from the signal and printed nothing to stdout. A script had nothing to parse and no message saying why. I wrote the new tests first and ran them on the current code: both failed, with the process killed by the signal and stdout empty. I posted that before-table on #1221 before changing any code.

The cause: yoyo only listened for SIGTERM, SIGHUP and SIGQUIT on piped text runs, so json runs kept the default behaviour and died mid-stream.

The fix: main.rs now marks json runs (not stream-json, not --print), and a small rule in src/prompt/sigterm.rs arms the listener for piped text runs or marked json runs. The existing text-mode filter isn't widened. main.rs's json branch already used the "was interrupted" state for is_error, the exit code and -o, so nothing else needed changing.

After the fix, I ran the built binary by hand after cargo build had finished (binary mtime 02:19:05), with an existing out.txt:

| signal | exit | stdout | is_error | response | out.txt |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| SIGTERM | 143 | one JSON object | true | the partial reply | unchanged |
| SIGHUP | 129 | same | true | same | unchanged |
| SIGQUIT | 131 | same | true | same | unchanged |
| SIGINT | 130 | same | true | same | unchanged |

Stderr also says (interrupted) and that out.txt was not written. I only ran SIGINT on the fixed binary. This change doesn't touch the Ctrl+C handling, but I didn't rebuild the old code to check SIGINT there.

Verification:
• New tests in tests/output_failed_run.rs: SIGTERM and SIGHUP cases check the exit code, that stdout is a single JSON object, is_error: true, the streamed partial text in response, the (interrupted) note, and that out.txt is byte-identical. A unit test checks that only json runs were added to the listener rule.
• Recall control: I put the old listener condition back with a NEUTERED marker (count 1 before running). Both new tests failed by name. After restoring it (count 0) they passed. The after-table and this result are on #1221.
• Full checks: cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings and the full cargo test all pass.

Other changes:
• docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md and single-prompt.md now describe what json mode does when interrupted. The stream-json sentence is unchanged and still true: it has no signal handler.
• The size limit for src/prompt.rs in tests/module_size.rs went from 3988 to 3992 lines (it was already at 3991 before this change).
